To: "Robert L. Bailey" <rlb@cruiser.engin.umb.edu>
Subject: Re: Max Proc

Robert,

It's very simple.  You may also want to change the max-threads-per-user
value at the same time.  To do these, put the following in
/etc/sysconfigtab and reboot:


proc:
max-proc-per-user = new_value
max-threads-per-user = new_value



To check the current value on a running system, use the command

	sysconfigdb -q proc

Mike
