From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Dec 06 20:13:51 1996
From: Neil Movold <nmovold () bsl ! bm>
Date: Fri, 06 Dec 1996 20:13:51 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Searching for FTP Mirroring Software for Digital UNIX V4.0
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076343421500

I have a need to replicate some FTP directories from several servers onto 
a few of my servers using FTP.  I have found a few programs to do this, 
but they are written for Linux and Solaris.  They were :

1) Easy-mirror (em-1.4) found at ftp.jags.co.uk
  

   This one looks really good, but it is in Linux form and Solaris.  I even
   tried to port it but there was too many problems doing that so I gave
   up.  I then tried Digital's Freeport software to port the Solaris
   binary, but it was V2.0 and freeport could only handle v1.n binaries.

2) Mirror

   I have heard of this one but it appears to be all Perl code which is
   fine as I write alot of perl code myself, but a real binary would be
   more preferred like EM is.

If anyone has any suggestions, I would greatly appreciate them.

			Neil :-)


