From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Dec 06 18:18:38 1996
From: tim_oconnor () uhlaw ! com
Date: Fri, 06 Dec 1996 18:18:38 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Modems:  using uugetty
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076343421499


I have installed a couple of Practical Peripherals modems (14.4)  on an   
Alpha 2000 using getty and all seems to be fine, but I need to dial out   
with at least one of the modems.  I used uugetty with the following   
inittab entry:

ttyd1:30:respawn:/usr/lib/uucp/uugetty -r -t /dev/ttyd1 M19200

This works fine, I can dial-in and dial out using kermit with no problem.   
   


My problem is uugetty respawns the process on this modem continuously   
rather than wait for a login.  This causes the /var/adm/wtmp to log the   
process and causes this file to grow very quickly causing the /usr   
partition to reach capacity.

I set the modem to disable modem echo thinking this might be the cause of   
the box not waiting for a login.  This did not work.

I checked the list archives and there is very little on uugetty.

btw:

here is my inittab entry when I use getty for the same modem,  this work   
without a problem.

ttyd1:30:respawn:/usr/sbin/getty /dev/ttyd1 M19200 vt100


Any Ideas?

TIA



Tim O'Connor
Accounting Programmer / Webmaster
