I had asked what a console message saying:

WARNING: too many porocessor corrected errors.  Reporting suspended.
Machine Check error corrected by processor

meant and what to do about it.  I had several people say that is was
probably a memory error and that a tool called DECevent could help solve
the problem much better than uerf could.  It is apparently available
with 3.2g and 4.x.  I must thank "Kurt Carlson
<sxkac@java.sois.alaska.edu>" who generously took my binary.errlog file
and ran it through DECEvent.

As it turns out, I was getting a "Bcache error" which DEC says is a CPU
parity error and they are going to replace the CPU card.

Thanks so much for all the help!

