From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Dec 04 09:25:33 1996
From: "Harinder Singh" <singhh () vrinet ! com>
Date: Wed, 04 Dec 1996 09:25:33 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: PASSWORD CLEAR AT CONSOLE LEVEL!
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076343421427

     MY ORIGINAL QUESTION::
     
     Hello all!
     
     We have DEC 2100 running Digital Unix 3.2C. We had set the password at 
     the console level (POO>>>). We have forgotten the password. How can we 
     clear the passowrd at the console level?
     
     We tried clearing it, but, it prompts us for the old password, which 
     we don't have. I tried set password too, but, that also prompts for 
     the old password.
     
     Any hep will be appreciated!!!
     
     Thanks
     
     Harry
     
     
     THE ANSWER IS AS FOLLOWS:
     
     From the document:
     
     AlphaServer 2x00, 2x00A
     Loadable Firmware Update Utility
     User Guide and Release Notes
     
     found in file /cdfs/DOC/ALPHA2100_V45_FW_RELNOTE.TXT;1
     
     o If you have forgotten the current password, use the login
     command in conjunction with the Halt button to clear the password, as 
     described below:
     
     1. Make sure the Halt button is in the "out" position (not
     lit).
     
     2. Enter the login command:
     
     P00>>> login
     
     3. When the Enter Password: prompt is displayed, press the
     Halt button (the button should light up), then press <Return>.
     
     4. Press the Halt button to the "out" position (not lit). The
     password is now cleared and the console cannot be put into secure mode 
     unless you set a new password.
     
     NOTE
     
     If you enter login with the Halt button in (lit), the command will 
     fail, even if you entered the correct password. This prevents an 
     intruder from depressing the Halt button and locking the front panel. 
     Also, if you leave the Halt button in (lit) after you clear the 
     password, the system will not boot.
     

